WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.160
- [Narrator] For the
first time in 50 years,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.820
Campbell's iconic soup can
looked different in 2021.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.580
Even though the changes are
subtle, it makes the can feel.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.900
- Like one that feels at home

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.300
in your pantry versus one
that you remember seeing

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.730
in grandma's or granddad's pantry.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.520
- M'm, m'm, good!
(playful music)

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.100
- So let's break down
Campbell's first major rebrand

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.470
in decades and how those small changes

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.270
are breathing new life into soup,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.250
the company's core product.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.930
The redesign is so slight

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.390
that customers might not
have even noticed it.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.560
- It was really important to hear

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.050
that Campbell's did this
evolutionary change,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.860
didn't step away from
their iconic look and feel.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.540
- This is Rob Meyerson,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.270
the founder of brand
strategy firm Heirloom.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.040
He's been studying Campbell's redesign

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.100
for a new edition of the book
"Designing Brand Identity."

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.920
Though Campbell's Soup Company
makes more than just soup,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.910
its namesake product has been
on shelves for 130 years.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.580
The label has been tweaked
many times since then

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.210
but only significantly
redesigned a handful of times,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.116
like in 1898 when the company
first chose the colors

00:01:03.116 --> 00:01:04.320
that would define it.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.020
- The red and white on
the can, which is inspired

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.720
by the Cornell football team's uniforms.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.130
- [Narrator] That red
and white wasn't touched

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.240
in the new redesign

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.800
but other elements were tweaked.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.810
For example, the new logo gets rid

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.600
of the drop shadow and
disconnects the letters.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.180
- Drop shadows are a little bit

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.820
of a relic of an era in design

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.120
where adding dimension
was seen as a positive.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.000
Removing any unnecessary components,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.210
like that subtle drop shadow
just puts all the more focus

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.980
on the recognizable assets.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.990
- [Narrator] The overall
effect is a simpler,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.060
more modern take on the logo.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.790
And modernizing is a theme
throughout the redesign.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.820
- The medallion, they
retained all of the text

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.780
and basically the same
imagery within the medallion

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.730
but they added some dimension to it

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.650
that looks a little bit more 3D.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.770
It pops a little bit more, it
feels brighter on the cans.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.770
The word soup has been
written in a different color.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.510
They've gone from a serif typeface,

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.080
which has these little feet
and pieces on the bottom

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.700
of the P, for example,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.830
and they've gone to
what's called sans serif

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.663
without a serif,

00:02:08.663 --> 00:02:11.340
and that's typically a
little bit more modern.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.260
They also retained this slant
on the interior of the O

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.960
and so I think this is
just striking a balance

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.050
between modernizing, refreshing,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.630
but keeping some recognizability

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.700
between the old can and the new can.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.680
- [Narrator] The company
did add something new,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.840
a picture of each soup's ingredients.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.630
- They've wanted to emphasize
the food ingredients

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.500
in the can.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.600
- [Narrator] Aaron Back is a
Wall Street Journal columnist

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.340
who covers all things Campbell's.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.100
- This is about reaching
young people who care

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.120
about food quality,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.680
who care about what
they're feeding their kids,

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.840
and saying, look, there's
real tomatoes in this.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.940
- [Narrator] And there's another
benefit to those pictures.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.710
- Instead of using a picture

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.070
of a bowl of soup or a spoon holding soup,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.400
they've gone with just this
simple shot of the ingredients,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.810
the piece of chicken and the noodles.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.790
And that alone makes them stand out

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.250
from everybody else in the space.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.600
- [Narrator] So why did the company go

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.570
through all this trouble
for a redesign so subtle?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.070
- The last thing you wanna do is make it

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:11.250
so that people don't recognize
your cans or your products.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.360
- [Narrator] And that Campbell's can

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.220
was already so recognizable

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.990
and had been for decades.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:19.620
It was memorialized by Andy
Warhol and in catchy ads.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.018
- [Announcer] Campbell's
Tomato Soup, m'm, m'm, good.

00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:22.851
- For a long time,

00:03:22.851 --> 00:03:26.430
Campbell's iconic status
translated into very strong sales.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.280
Around the turn of this
century, that came to an end

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.930
and they started running into problems.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.050
- [Narrator] Soup sales began
a steady decline for years.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.540
- The overwhelming perception
among young consumers

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.570
is that Campbell's soups
were old-fashioned,

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.270
unhealthy, out of style, and unappealing.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.470
- [Narrator] Changing that was part

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:47.520
of CEO Mark Clouse's new
strategy to prioritize soups

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.710
after years of expanding beyond it.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.390
Some of that expansion worked.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.190
Campbell's Snack division now accounts

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.250
for nearly half of the
company's sales, but fresh foods

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.310
like baby carrots and
salsa were less successful.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.410
The company ultimately sold its entire

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.960
refrigerated food unit in 2019.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.940
- The insight of the
new management was look,

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.800
the name of the company is
Campbell's Soup Company.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.510
It's our most important product.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.650
- [Narrator] So the company tried

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.540
to appeal to younger consumers

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.660
by refreshing both the
label and the recipes.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.190
- They took out high fructose corn syrup

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.900
from the condensed soup line.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.790
The cream of mushroom,
cream of chicken soups

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.110
now have more fresh cream in them.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.910
- [Narrator] The company
also tried new marketing,

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.740
like sponsoring an episode of "Top Chef."

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.450
- Gonna do a Swiss chard gratin.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.710
- [Narrator] Making an NFT

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.740
and partnering with the Madden NFL game.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.360
And so far it's helped.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.520
Soup sales have grown in recent years.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.390
That's in part due

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.845
to the pandemic when more
people were cooking at home.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:41.010
♪ And it's magic. ♪

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.470
- [Narrator] But those lockdown
customers stuck around.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.660
- Campbell, you know, not
too long ago, was viewed

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.090
as one of the most troubled
of the major food brands.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.010
But last year was one
of the top performers.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.960
Its stock went up to 31%,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.390
and that was in an overall
down year for the stock market.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.710
- [Narrator] Still, the future of growth

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.770
for Campbell's isn't just
in soup, it's snacks.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.810
The company designates
that division's role

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.390
as accelerated growth,
but it was important

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.690
for Campbell's to staunch
its core products bleeding.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.130
- Once you clean up the product

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.070
and also make the label
look more appealing,

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.650
what you do is you kind of
give a permission structure.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.150
That's something you can
maybe even be excited

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.890
about to have a can

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.225
of Campbell's tomato soup in your pantry.

00:05:19.225 --> 00:05:21.892
(pensive music)

